# Every real, deployed config/{component}/* file (settings.json,
# ofelia-config.ini, rabbitmq.conf, etc.) carries live credentials or
# host-specific values -- only its checked-in *.example template belongs
# in the repo. Wildcarded, not enumerated per filename, so a new
# component's config never needs a line added here (matches docs/.gitignore's
# components/*.md wildcard for the same reason).
config/*/*
!config/*/*.example

# rabbitmq/redis bind-mounted runtime data (docker-compose.core.yaml) --
# host-local persisted state, not something to check in.
data/
